          <li class="flex items-start"><i class="fa-solid fa-check text-gold mt-1 mr-3"></i><span><strong>Bali's Premier Training Grounds:</strong> Discover why sites like the USAT Liberty Wreck in Tulamben, the currents of Nusa Penida, and the macro-bays of Amed provide the perfect challenges to forge professional skills.</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start"><i class="fa-solid fa-check text-gold mt-1 mr-3"></i><span><strong>Prerequisites & Duration:</strong> Get a clear checklist of what you need before you start (Rescue Diver, 40+ dives) and realistic timelines, typically ranging from 4 to 12 weeks for a thorough internship.</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start"><i class="fa-solid fa-check text-gold mt-1 mr-3"></i><span><strong>Beyond Certification:</strong> Gain insights into career opportunities, from guiding in Bali to working on liveaboards worldwide after you qualify.</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start"><i class="fa-solid fa-check text-gold mt-1 mr-3"></i><span><strong>Budgeting for Pro Training:</strong> Learn to navigate the costs, including a breakdown of course fees, PADI materials, equipment considerations, accommodation, and daily living expenses.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-lightblue"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-shield mr-2"></i>The Divemaster Role: More Than Just a Great Diver</h3>
        <p>Becoming a Divemaster means becoming a leader. The certification qualifies you to supervise scuba diving activities and assist instructors with student divers. The training is designed to develop your problem-solving abilities, risk management skills, and situational awareness. Your days will be spent honing skills like dive site mapping, delivering effective briefings, managing dive logistics, and perfecting your demonstration-quality rescue and skill circuits.</p>

        <h3 class="text-lightblue"><i class="fa-solid fa-map-location-dot mr-2"></i>Choosing Your Training Ground: Bali's Diverse Underwater Classroom</h3>
        <p>A quality Divemaster program in Bali leverages the island's incredible diversity to build adaptable, confident professionals. Your training isn't confined to a single bay. Expect to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Master Logistics in Tulamben:</strong> Practice guiding certified divers and mapping a complex site at the world-famous USAT Liberty Shipwreck.</li>
            <li><strong>Conquer Currents in Nusa Penida:</strong> Learn to manage groups in challenging conditions while drift diving with majestic Manta Rays and searching for the elusive Mola Mola.</li>
            <li><strong>Refine Finesse in Amed & Padang Bai:</strong> Perfect your buoyancy and macro-spotting skills while leading divers through vibrant coral gardens and muck diving sites.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This variety ensures you graduate not just with a certification card, but with real-world experience across a spectrum of diving scenarios.</p>

        <h3 class="text-accent" id="faq"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-question mr-2"></i>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
