          <span class="font-semibold">What are the prerequisites for the Divemaster course?</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-sm"></i>
        </button>
        <div class="hidden mt-3 text-white/80">To begin, you must be at least 18 years old, be a certified Rescue Diver, have a current EFR Primary and Secondary Care certification (or equivalent) within the last 24 months, have at least 40 logged dives, and provide a medical statement signed by a physician within the last 12 months.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 bg-white/5">
        <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
          <span class="font-semibold">How much does a Divemaster course cost in Bali?</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-sm"></i>
        </button>
        <div class="hidden mt-3 text-white/80">Costs vary between dive centers but typically range from $1,000 to $2,500 USD. Be sure to ask what's included. Key costs to check are PADI fees, learning materials, equipment rental, and the number of dives. Some programs offer accommodation packages.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 bg-white/5">
        <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
          <span class="font-semibold">Can I work as a Divemaster in Bali after getting certified?</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-sm"></i>
        </button>
        <div class="hidden mt-3 text-white/80">Working legally in Indonesia requires a specific work permit (KITAS), which dive centers must sponsor. While opportunities exist, they are competitive. The best approach is to excel during your training, network, and demonstrate a professional attitude.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 bg-white/5">
        <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
          <span class="font-semibold">What is the best time of year for Divemaster training in Bali?</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-sm"></i>
        </button>
        <div class="hidden mt-3 text-white/80">Diving in Bali is excellent year-round. However, the dry season (April to November) generally offers the calmest sea conditions and best visibility, making it ideal for intensive training. The Mola Mola season (typically July-October) also provides unique guiding challenges and experiences.</div>
